Description: Expose Flurry's existing perspective camera and trail depths to OpenGL
 Flurry projects its 3D particles on the CPU. Preserve the original disabled
 path and supply an ordinary perspective camera when Enable 3D is active.
 The layer renders the two views; no eye offsets or duplicate simulation live
 in the saver. Original settings and the BSD licence remain unchanged.
Author: Daniel Ramos
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-10-14

--- a/hacks/glx/flurry.h
+++ b/hacks/glx/flurry.h
@@ -106,6 +106,7 @@
         floatToVector seraphimVertices[NUMSMOKEPARTICLES*2+1];
         floatToVector seraphimColors[NUMSMOKEPARTICLES*4+1];
 	float seraphimTextures[NUMSMOKEPARTICLES*2*4];
+        float cameraVertices[NUMSMOKEPARTICLES*4][3];
 } SmokeV;
 
 void InitSmoke(SmokeV *s);
